window.PICKR_BOOKS = {"echoes":{"title":"Echoes of Life","by":"Dan Engström","pub":"Piratpensionat Produktion","year":"2025","about":"Short poems on noticing, connection, doubt and resistance, with four sonnets, The Edge of Perception, at their heart.","blocks":[["h",1,"Foreword","foreword",1],["p","This is not an instruction manual. ",0],["p","It is a collection of echoes—of snatches of thoughts, of glimpses, questions, and moments. Written in the in-between, in that fleeting space where something sensed becomes something tangible in the mind, on paper and perhaps even shared. Where language is a tool and a means to an end, but also where words are poignant and have a beauty of their own. Where we reach in vain towards explaining vague discomfort or elusive ideas. Where the painstakingly chosen word can trace the outline of experience, but never define it.",0],["p",[["At the heart of this book are four sonnets under the umbrella title ",0],["The Edge of Perception",1],[". Together, they explore what it means to notice, imagine, reinterpret, and create. These four phases are my experience of creating. Of seeing something, reimagining it. Of trying to make sense of it and give it a body of its own, and then the fear of letting it go. Each of these four sonnets – how I do love a sonnet – stands on its own, yet together they form a prism, or four windows into a single space of creation. They shift the perspective, offering different angles, which maybe allows us to see the familiar in unfamiliar ways. The main question is what if.",0]],0],["p","Around these four sonnets are other poems—short and long, playful and serious, grounded and untethered. They’re not arranged to explain a thesis. They’re here to resonate. To touch. To invite. The four themes are an afterthought, umbrellas over what the poems mean to me, which might be altogether nonsense to you. Read them from start to finish or dive into one or the other as your fancy takes you, and make up your own mind. ",0],["p","What you find here may not be what I was thinking as I wrote these poems. But if you meet a phrase that lingers, a rhythm that reverberates in your mind, or a phrase that tells you something, then perhaps we’ve shared a moment. If you do, I am happy we met through these pages, however briefly. Maybe that shared moment is the whole point.",0],["p","Billdal, Sweden, March 25th, 2025",0],["p","— Dan ",0],["h",1,"The Edge of Perception","the-edge-of-perception",0],["p",[["Four perspectives on imagination, curiosity and creation, tracing four phases of creation. ",1]],1],["h",2,"Discovery","discovery",0],["s",0,["The rugs are ships in a sea of fire","Those are the rules, and without exception","Dad, were there really pirates for hire?","Must have earned them a YEAR of detention"]],["s",4,["Every little piece leads him somewhere new","Rugs are ships to shore on a burning floor","Facts are only facts if you think they’re true","You said pirates were rugged once before"]],["s",8,["Listen dad, just chill, he said later on","Trying too hard prevents me from seeing","My self-conscious mind is not so much gone","As keenly alive by simply just being"]],["s",12,["Our floors may burn, our socks may smoulder","That’s still in the eyes of the beholder"]],["h",2,"Vertigo","vertigo",0],["s",14,["There is a house in a forest somewhere","A man had to bring it there on his back","The building became his food, drink and air","With ev’ry brick, ev’ry stick, ev’ry sack"]],["s",18,["Touching the sky, his infinity room","Impossible proportions so chosen","To perfectly fit. I wonder to whom","Does it cater, this music so frozen"]],["s",22,["To see pines from above; tall trees and proud,","Stretching towards you, frustrated, in vain,","Is that why he built this personal cloud,","For new perspectives, again and again?"]],["s",26,["Precarious views from heaven’s shoulder","And yet, in the eyes of the beholder"]],["h",2,"Chisel","chisel",0],["s",28,["The canvas is blank, the music unplayed","All that hard work to end up in a loss","This particular piece never took shape","However brilliant she thought it was"]],["s",32,["Suddenly, at the edge of perception","Something flies, she is taken by surprise","A different idea, craving for attention","So it begins, she hangs on for dear life"]],["s",36,["It might turn out elegant, or bold","She never has a say in the matter","No matter. She enjoys doing what she’s told","Searching for meaning, mad as a hatter"]],["s",40,["Whether her search gets warmer or colder","Is left in the eyes of the beholder"]],["h",2,"Reckoning","reckoning",0],["s",42,["How is your creation coming along?","Asked the older god while stirring his tea","Well, I’m not sure I’m not doing it wrong","Said the younger god; My humans can’t see"]],["s",46,["He shrugged. Lots of humans yet to be born.","She frowned. I’d like to chase the dark away","I’ve come up with a concept I call dawn","Time would be either night or, maybe, day?"]],["s",50,["That’s great, he said. No linear time, just round","Yes, she said, but what if they don’t like it","Another shrug. Don’t you know what you’ve found?","Your call, but it’s cool, you can’t deny it"]],["s",54,["So let there be light, that’s what he told her","Straight in the eye of any beholder"]],["h",1,"Perception and Curiosity","perception-and-curiosity",0],["p",[["The act of noticing, the seed of observation, and the joy and awe of actively taking a surprising perspective, seeing the world with new eyes and reinterpreting what comes to mind.",1]],1],["h",2,"Poetry","poetry",0],["s",56,["Pebbles in a pond, pearls gently dropped","Sending circles of single waves","Patiently and purposely prompted by thoughts","That were slowly and silently sinking out of reach","To lift up life into light from the depths"]],["h",2,"My rogue mind","my-rogue-mind",0],["s",61,["My mind creates the strangest things","It works like that, on its own","Eerie places fit for kings","The queen of bus stops on her throne"]],["s",65,["If you will note that something’s pink","Then I’ll imagine it’s blue","Make a claim and I will think","What if the opposite were true?"]],["h",2,"The Fringe of reality","the-fringe-of-reality",0],["s",69,["I am an elusive idea","Turning my collar to the rain","This is the fringe of reality","Did the sign say Awareness, 3 miles on?","Only poetry can bring me home"]],["h",2,"No title","no-title",0],["s",74,["The forest goes silent at dusk;","A parallel world under still water -","I watch myself while the light lasts"]],["h",2,"Transitions","transitions",0],["s",77,["The last rays of the day briefly visit a glade;","Trees turn loudly to gold, grass to roaring fires -","A moment later, silence"]],["h",2,"Birds","birds",0],["s",80,["Birds don’t ask to try","If they do, they die"]],["s",82,["Birds don’t stop to think","Their instinct is to fly"]],["h",2,"Winter solstice","winter-solstice",0],["s",84,["Just when our patience runs out","The sun gently kisses the rocks","and springs back up -","Suddenly, the stillness brings hope"]],["h",1,"Identity and Connection","identity-and-connection",0],["p",[["The relational self  – how we become through connections with others. From companionship, kinship, and love to lives lived.",1]],1],["h",2,"To a friend","to-a-friend",0],["s",88,["Even when we met that first time I could tell","Meeting is a breath we take before farewell","From our first hello to our last goodbye","You never let us go, never questioned why","It would leave its mark, your life of open doors","You were part of ours, but we were all of yours"]],["s",94,["For noone but you","We stood out from the crowd","We’ll see each other through","I hope we did you proud"]],["h",2,"This is yours","this-is-yours",0],["s",98,["I see it, she said with a shrug and a smile","Well we don’t, frowned I, we could use your eye","Feel free to explain what you see in your dreams","I cannot, she sighed, but here’s how it feels","That future is faint. It’s a wish, not a fate","that you must accept. It’s yours to create."]],["h",2,"Ohana","ohana",0],["s",104,["Strangers in the crowd, yet siblings by default","Silent understanding, sweet but dearly bought","Your power and your drive just as strong as mine","I share your doubts and fear of failure by design"]],["s",108,["The waters are so dark, out of breath by fright","A lonely stretch of road in the dying night"]],["s",110,["But listen, we’re alive! There still might be a chance","Just keep moving forward, that’s how we advance","Remember your tattoo; no mountain we can’t climb","One stroke, one step, one perfect moment at a time"]],["h",2,"Afterwards","afterwards",0],["s",114,["On a summer evening, the five friends meet again","The ancient wall cools their backs","The setting sun is warm on their faces","Relieved laughter hides their stunned silence"]],["h",2,"Years and years","years-and-years",0],["s",118,["The birds are still at the end of the day","The sky is deeply violet and blue","The tides of time have swept them both away","Long ago they lost everyone they knew"]],["s",122,["A lifetime shared, once upon a time","He, smoothing another crease in her brow","She, bearing him from flawed to the sublime","They did so but who remembers them now"]],["s",126,["As evening falls they are still together","Gently holding hands in eternal June","A subtle scent of honey from the heather","Walking in a glade by the Braemalune"]],["s",130,["Still today, in that glade they meet again","It is never fully dark, even then"]],["h",2,"Spring","spring",0],["s",132,["I realised winter is dying","Just now, with the first hint of spring","Come temperate winds, gently sighing!","Come new life, about to begin"]],["s",136,["As darkness speaks of dawn behind us","The skeins of birds that flew","Will soon return and thus remind us","That life begins anew"]],["s",140,["As signs of hope and joy set free","A million birds will sing","From winter’s muted hills and trees","Like every year in spring"]],["s",144,["We long for those we’ve lost and grieve","I think of us and smile","That friends like us still love and breathe","So very much alive"]],["h",2,"Fathering","fathering",0],["s",148,["I know that look of hers, my bad","It’s all on me, again","Just hang in there, when you’re the dad","You mustn’t show the strain"]],["s",152,["Displeasured eyes are déja vu","Best shut up, but you won’t","Deeply frustrated if you do","Quickly snubbed if you don’t"]],["s",156,["It’s funny you felt lost at sea","Beside her as she grew","You took it on yourself but she","Was always there for you"]],["h",2,"Path to Exile","path-to-exile",0],["s",160,["The man I saw walking to the station","He sported Path to Exile cross his chest","As if Exile was a destination","An active choice, in earnest or in jest"]],["s",164,["Might it show political persuasion","Or could it be an author’s famous quote","Maybe he was setting demarcations","His stony face forbidding and remote"]],["s",168,["And then again it also sounds like fun","Maybe Path to Exile just make games","A friendly crew who welcome everyone","The cutting edge, just shy to flaunt their names"]],["s",172,["So maybe I was wrong, it’s hard to call","If he was smiling at me after all"]],["h",1,"Doubt and Becoming","doubt-and-becoming",0],["p",[["Of the self-doubt of becoming, of the fears, joys and power of transitions. ",1]],1],["h",2,"Pantoum","pantoum",0],["s",174,["To have Steinbeck’s words running through my head","Even the best laid plans of mice and men","Often go awry. Might just stay in bed.","Another lost foothold, time and again"]],["s",178,["Even the best laid plans of mice and men","Brief releases of tensions in the mind","Another lost foothold, time and again","Searching yet dreading what else I will find"]],["s",182,["Brief releases of tensions in the mind","Often go awry. Might just stay in bed.","Searching yet dreading what else I will find","To have Steinbeck’s words running through my head"]],["h",2,"Poetry II","poetry-ii",0],["s",186,["The painstakingly preferred, almost perfect word","Instantly invoking impressions in the mind, burning images left behind","The rhythm and the rhyme, slanted yet sublime","A moment of deeper dedication allowing for a different interpretation","Distractedly dwelling on a different spelling","Laughing at leaning towards a lewd new meaning"]],["s",192,["Like time turns winter into spring, words would transform anything","Verses to highlight the whole wretchedness of a human soul, or","Opening eyes unseeing to the unlikely experience of being"]],["h",2,"Letting go","letting-go",0],["s",195,["A sudden thought; that’s it, you’re done","Don’t want to see it through","You brush it off, you’ve just begun","And this is what you do"]],["s",199,["Who are you to fold and quit","At the drop of a hat","Lower the mask just when it fits","You know better than that"]],["s",203,["Challenge yourself is what you preach","Succeed and take a bow","But tasks that made you have to reach","Are second nature now"]],["s",207,["The efforts made, the things you’ve seen","The lessons over time","You’re letting them become routine","What mountains now to climb"]],["s",211,["Respect yourself and all that work","Feel free to drop that smirk","Embrace the need to lose control","Inside your restless soul"]],["h",2,"Rewards","rewards",0],["s",215,["Alarm goes off just after four","You stretch and yawn and sigh","In half an hour you’re out the door","The bed is warm and dry"]],["s",219,["Preparing for that epic day","You said it’s up to me","To do the work, and come what may","Just not today, said he"]],["s",223,["You’ve made your plans, now see them through","Enjoy them while they last","In support, making sure you do","The ghost of sessions past"]],["s",227,["Preparing with that day ahead","Something you’re forced to do","That’s why you’d rather stay in bed","Again, that’s up to you"]],["s",231,["That day is not a bill to pay","No river you must ford","It’s not a mountain in your way","That day is your reward"]],["h",2,"The Hike towards the Top","the-hike-towards-the-top",0],["s",235,["The hills were green, the sky was blue","Our packs were stuffed with gear","I led and left the others to","Boldly bring up the rear"]],["s",239,["They took another break, again","Before we reached the top","Come, said I, leaning on my cane","This is no place to stop"]],["s",243,["Calm down, said Michael, on all fours","This climb might take a year","We’ve had it with this hill of yours","My God, I need a beer"]],["s",247,["I know, I said, this hike is steep","But try to keep awake","It doesn’t help to fall asleep","On every rest you take"]],["s",251,["Ellie asked What’s the point again?","She liked it down below","That lovely little shaded glen","Why did we have to go?"]],["s",255,["You asked for change and something new","I said and spread my hands","You need to move to see the view","A child would understand"]],["s",259,["But most of them were now done in","They turned and started down","I guess to where we were before","If not, then back to town"]],["s",263,["Three of us went on towards the top","John said If it were me","If I had quit or had to stop","I’d wonder what I’d see"]],["s",267,["You know I wouldn’t really mind","To learn that we were wrong","For that one chance the toil and grind","Was worth it all along"]],["h",2,"It was once","it-was-once",0],["s",271,["- We were lucky the rain ruined the play","Said the woman while looking for her seat","They called it off, but I went anyway","Noone here to talk to, nothing much to eat","Then you turned up, a puppy gone astray","You thought I looked stunning, I said you were sweet","How was it that we never got the note?","You know, the show is off, cancelled she wrote"]],["s",279,["- That seat was yours, he said, right over there","- This one? I’m amazed that you remember","- Of course. I can picture it anywhere","The cotton dress, so deep into September","The face, the eyes, the hair. My God, the hair!","That lonely girl, I just had to befriend her","- So that was me? Miss Too-good-to-be-true?","- Not really, he laughed, but I thought I could make do"]],["s",287,["Had the play been on I could have passed you by","There should have been an audience, a crowd","But we were there alone, just you and I","Your mock applause and jeers were really loud","At the empty stage, open to the sky","Even then I wanted to make you proud","- She smiled: I might have looked good, I guess","But I was just a girl, trying to impress"]],["s",295,["Breaking his thoughts, a woman by his side","- Hello old man, she said, come to see the show?","Is this seat taken, I mean occupied?","- It was, he said, once - sixty years ago","I can hear her now, some time before she died","- You really must move on, dear. It’s hard, I know","There will come a time when we both have passed away","Remember we were lucky to have the rain ruin our day"]],["h",1,"Society and Resistance","society-and-resistance",0],["p",[["Grounded in a transient world, on observing or resisting shifts and systems, and the tension between conformity and critique. Or perhaps just images of a life.",1]],1],["h",2,"To the young","to-the-young",0],["s",303,["Young were the kings, the makers and doers","Vigour was treasured in a simpler time","Of hunters and millers and bakers and brewers","Before the shift to this sordid paradigm"]],["s",307,["Ruling today are old friends of the wealthy","Power is treasured, crimes are forgiven,","The truth is a lie, while blindness is healthy","State what you have; it shall be thee given"]],["s",311,["The wheels are in motion. It is time to be","Agile and brave, no one’s powerful friend","When hoodies and Red Bull trump suits and Chablis","Beware, sitting ducks, it’s the eve of the end"]],["s",315,["Awake, restless souls, there are new open doors","To scented spaces, blessed with myrrh and gold","If you dare enter, the world will be yours","Haste to adopt it; before it is sold"]],["s",319,["Reject the authority of the content","Refuse any order that stifles dissent","Retire the silence that dictates consent","So reshape the world that your fathers have bent"]],["h",2,"Retort to the old","retort-to-the-old",0],["s",323,["We crashed it, now it’s up to you","A film we’ve seen before","Why don’t you stop and think it through","Since when are we your whore"]],["s",327,["A generation set apart","Together or alone","A hundred million beating hearts","These queens don’t need your thrones"]],["s",331,["It’s not on us to save your realm","To build or to forgive","It’s not on us to take the helm","We just want to live"]],["s",335,["We won’t create your wonderland","I almost wish you’d understand"]],["h",2,"Keeping you safe","keeping-you-safe",0],["s",337,["Throbbing in my ears reassures me I’m alive","Early night in Stockholm, nineteen sixtynine","Chanel in tiny vials, always number five","Just get out of here, the kid will be just fine"]],["s",341,["Voices out of reach, wond’ring who they are","Really hard to tell, they’re old and sound the same","I feel my pulse beat out a syncopated bar","A secret noone knows; that rhythm sings my name"]],["s",345,["A door somewhere slams shut, the echo fades away","I get this sudden urge to find my yellow socks","Too scary in the dark, I’d better try by day","Make sure to stash your stuff well inside the box"]],["s",349,["This will keep you safe. That will help you shine.","Just get out of here, this kid will be just fine"]],["h",2,"Next stop:","next-stop",0],["s",351,["Her tone is soft, not easy to ignore","The many calls which stop is next in line","When I should start to head towards the door","If we are running late or right on time"]],["s",355,["It’s good to hear her automated voice","I’m comforted by all the stops and maps","Always there to help me make my choice","To journey on, or to get off perhaps"]],["s",359,["I’ll get to my desired location","Free from worry, completely safe and sound","Thanks to her, I’ll reach my destination","I only have to know where I am bound"]],["s",363,["But life resists, it won’t be thus defined","There is no map of bus stops in my mind"]],["h",2,"Façades","fa-ades",0],["s",365,["I drove through someone’s suburb once","But wasn’t too impressed","By all its gardens neatly trimmed","And people smartly dressed"]],["s",369,["Expensive cars and skateboard kids","Appearing well-behaved","The only mark of discontent;","A sign that Jesus saves"]],["s",373,["Tapping to the rhythm of this","Frozen Dutch ballet of","Clones of prefab houses, I","Prepared to speed away"]],["s",377,["It’s too clean to be real, I thought","While looking for some sign","Of life in one pathetic home;","And realised it’s mine"]],["h",2,"Someone’s digging holes in my city","someone-s-digging-holes-in-my-city",0],["s",381,["Someone’s digging holes in my city","My hometown is pockmarked with sites","To me this place used to look pretty","Now there’s rubble where there were lights"]],["s",385,["They claim that the closures are needed","For now, for our city to grow","And then we have somehow succeeded?","Just how I am sure I don’t know"]],["s",389,["The people you meet look dejected","I miss when I heard my friends laugh","Before all the cranes were erected","Puking concrete on our behalf"]],["s",393,["You ask what is bringing me down?","There are holes all over my town"]],["h",2,"Dignity","dignity",0],["s",395,["Look at that, I said, how the place is packed","   We were young, and many, and strong","Before the fall, with poise and faith intact","   When all we could do was belong","We knew that only the lazy got sacked","   Unaware that something was wrong"]],["s",401,["Treasured at home and valued at the yard","Such a beautiful life, worthwhile but hard"]],["s",403,["Then whispers and rumours of changes to come","   Staying busy living my life","It’s best not to worry, try to stay numb","   The talk is that layoffs are rife","A limited job is better than none","   Lost my job, the house, then the wife"]],["s",409,["Your pride is the first thing that disappears","But breaking apart completely takes years"]],["s",411,["Music and laughter from somewhere next door","   Reflections of light ’cross the street","Strange, muffled rhythms I’ve not heard before","   I silently tap to the beat","Resigned to this feeling, don’t mind anymore","   A drink and a smoke would be sweet"]],["s",417,["A shell of a man, a lonely cliché","Blood on the ground as they take me away"]],["h",2,"On every morning light the dark descends","on-every-morning-light-the-dark-descends",0],["s",419,["We set our goals and quickly add some more","Owners of the world, we are birds of prey","For everyone, as we have learned before","We’re mice, we’re kings; and life gets in our way"]],["s",423,["Despair will fade at dawn when night must end","He boldly said, when he had seen it through","On every morning light the dark descends","A silent dragon that we never slew"]],["s",427,["While every day brings hope, we wake up scared","A thousand tasks to face, we mustn’t fail","We do, but smile, pretend we never cared","Another breath; remember to exhale"]],["s",431,["In our minds, waiting calmly in the wings","The sordid end, the brewing doom of kings"]],["h",2,"I never fail","i-never-fail",0],["s",433,["I never fail. I succeed, or I learn.","At first glance, that looks easy, does it not?","It’s hard when your hopes are all overturned","Bravado can truly cost you a lot"]],["s",437,["Successes are earned away from the light","Alone and in doubt, where demons will lurk","It’s not on the day you put up the fight","Deep down you know you should have done the work"]],["s",441,["But here you are now, it is what it is","A comfortable couch, so cosy and slack","With horizons to touch. Now tell me this","Dear friend, how bad do you need to bounce back?"]],["s",445,["Your many reasons will not justify","That you never made the effort to try"]],["h",2,"Maybe","maybe",0],["p","August 29th, 2024",0],["s",448,["Little waves gently greet the shore;","I wait patiently for inspiration -","The sun is hot on my skin","My bath robe cloaks my indecision"]]]},"hearts":{"title":"Hearts Around the Fire","by":"Dan Engström","pub":"Piratpensionat Produktion","year":"2026","about":"Bælwythe, an imagined town at a river's bend, told through the voices of the people who live there.","blocks":[["h",1,"OUR HOME BY THE RIVER","our-home-by-the-river",1],["p","Welcome to Bælwythe. Now sitting comfortably at the river’s bend, hugged by the hills and fields, the ruins of its walls tell a story of a dramatic, ancient past.",0],["p","Passing its gates, walking along its alleys, I hear soft murmurs in the air. I see no one. But there are people here–and they have voices, distinct voices. Sometimes they whisper, but more often I hear them talking in small groups as they go about their daily business. They debate and argue. ",0],["p","Sometimes, there is song, or at least rhythm. The rhythm of the blacksmith’s hammer, of night and day or the rhythm of the seasons, so important for the livelihood of the people in the town. There are shouts from the market, the rights to which were dearly bought from the king when the town was little but a hamlet.",0],["p","A little while ago, I entered through the East gate on a Thursday morning. It occurred to me that I still hear echoes of the voices of the dead, soft but clear as trumpets. The whisper that they once were here. They worked and loved, and fought and failed. Only now, I hear them through the voices of the living, of my contemporaries. We are the same. We feel the same. We work and we fail, but still we carry on, as they did. We still have the need to gather around the hearth and open our hearts to one another. We still are both fire and ice. ",0],["p","Only time sets us apart from them.",0],["p","And suddenly, thoughts at the very edge of perception are made tangible.",0],["p","Bælwythe needs not my nod of approval. It is not created. ",0],["p","It was there all along—unseen, unsung, in the dark. ",0],["p","Poetry simply turned on the lights.",0],["p","Billdal, July 2nd, 2026",0],["p","Dan Engström",0],["h",1,"THE HEARTH","the-hearth",0],["h",2,"The Town","the-town",0],["h",3,"Act I","act-i",0],["s",0,["Through chalky fields the river finds the sea","A man in weathered hat decides to stay","Picks up his axe and eyes the woods and bay","This river’s bend shall be a home to me"]],["s",4,["For fuel and fish, and game that’s roaming free","The builders come from near and far away","Some honest men, some sinners as they may","The fishermen tie vessels to the quay"]],["s",8,["Then rules and rulers, then the hang-man’s hill","Lurking at the edge of the village green","The church is small yet dominates the square","The hearths and homes put down at owner’s will","The refuse reek where flowers once had been","The rich prefer their houses to have stairs"]],["h",3,"Act II","act-ii",0],["s",14,["So many poor","Buildings reaching higher","Make sure you bar your doors","Then famine and the fire","Songs of ruin from the choir"]],["h",3,"Act III","act-iii",0],["s",19,["The streets return to life but now they're broad","Straight and paved and wide, like the plans they laid","With life renewed the cries of anguish fade","There is a bridge where once there was a ford"]],["s",23,["The boats come back with families on board","The merchants too, and makers to persuade","The blacksmith finds the tools that he had made","The builder’s hammer, and the soldier’s sword"]],["s",27,["With every step the silent tensions rise","When he is gone this land might well be mine","The builder’s tools, the sword the blacksmith found","The choice of which to wield, so say the wise","To build or to protect, to do or die","A pocket of communion makes a town"]],["h",2,"Bælwythe","baelwythe",0],["s",33,["The morning mists rise gently from the surface","Meandering, the river hugs the downs","Its course is a caress of fields and meadows","Before arriving at the edge of town"]],["s",37,["My Bælwythe, lovely Bælwythe on the water","Your leaping stone securing North to South","From weary huntsmen hiking past the hilltops","To ships come sailing from the river’s mouth"]],["s",41,["They come to sell their lambswool at the market","They come to buy the monastery’s cheese","They come to trade, they come to beg for breadcrumbs","While some will dine on boar and roasted geese"]],["s",45,["The singing in the summer from the taverns","The clang of hammers from the blacksmith’s shop","To climb the icy stairs of the cathedral","And feel the winter winds there at the top"]],["s",49,["To walk along your streets of brick and mortar","To wander past your homes of open doors","Oh Bælwythe, while your stones may rest from conflict,","How will you make the future promise yours?"]],["h",1,"THE HEARTS","the-hearts",0],["h",2,"The Teacher","the-teacher",0],["s",53,["Gather ’round, come closer to the fire","See the sparks rise effortlessly higher","The way, sweet one, you feel the heat has grown","One day, I’m sure, will help you make your own","It’s fine, young man, if you’re not fond of me","My mission is to teach you to be free"]],["s",59,["And you my friend, with fire in your eyes","Who so reject the darkness and the lies","Those embers have glowed since the dawn of time","The guardian’s torch—for a while—is mine","Ever it burns to shine on what is true","If you so yearn I’ll pass it on to you"]],["h",2,"The Dyer","the-dyer",0],["s",65,["I straighten out a tiny crease,","Feeling the fabric of the fleece","The touch of the palm of my hand","Takes stock of every single strand","The way it speaks and how it reads,","The cloth will tell me what it needs"]],["s",71,["An image forms inside my mind","Of soul and colour intertwined","Both earthy brown or crimson red","Sing clear to me inside my head"]],["s",75,["With each new fabric that is dyed","Each cloth transformed with worker’s pride","By all the stories they will tell","The dyer is transformed as well"]],["h",2,"The Merchant","the-merchant",0],["s",79,["The pride that fills a day of honest toil","To find fatigue fits well upon your brow","To nurture needs like farmers work the soil","Your pledge to help—the merchant’s ox and plough—","Will find your treasure while you fathom how","To grow your fortune, fail and try anew","At rest, at night, to know it’s up to you"]],["h",2,"The Thief","the-thief",0],["s",86,["The boots step softly on the stone","In silence to the door","They fall like snowflakes silently","As they have done before"]],["s",90,["A thief deserves a thief they say","I’ll even out the score","Enjoy the rich man’s righteous rest","Like you have done before"]],["s",94,["You sleep on riches from the poor","A sordid little scene","If thief I am then thug are you","As you have ever been"]],["s",98,["A shadow in the dark I creep","Faceless ’cross your floor","The smell of fear is foul in here","As it has been before"]],["s",102,["Never doubt what they will do","We are as we are seen","Vile are you while thief am I","As we have ever been"]],["h",2,"The Healer","the-healer",0],["s",106,["Whisper me your woes, well I will receive you","Tally me your tears, trust me then to treat them","Point out to me the pain that you perceive"]],["s",109,["A hundred heartbeats saved for humankind","A thousand aches and pains are thus brought down"]],["s",111,["The healer still will hold internal doubt","For every fevered fear I face in here","The odds increase this one will never leave"]],["s",114,["I hold a secret hope","That you are not the one"]],["h",2,"The Brewer","the-brewer",0],["s",116,["In the beginning there was beer","So fine, the yield of yeast that year","Even then, before creation","The sweet scent of fermentation"]],["s",120,["He smiled and loosed the loudest laugh","Yes, that could be my epitaph","I jest with Genesis, and how","Just know that I refuse to bow","When life is hard and death is near","Nothing as holy as a beer"]],["s",126,["Peaceful, pious prayer for you, monk","I toast the courage of the drunk"]],["h",2,"The Blacksmith","the-blacksmith",0],["s",128,["The blows on the anvil ringing","The echoes keen and cold","The ancient song from forges past","The rhythm takes its hold"]],["s",132,["Some time ago he set his course","A life to learn his skill","To heat and hammer, thus to bend","The metal to his will"]],["s",136,["The clang by iron hammer cuts","The silence briefly slain","The sky will quickly seal its wound","Then shatter once again"]],["s",140,["The blacksmith masters metals thus","He triumphs in the end","Resistance thrives on burning rage","This fever is his friend"]],["s",144,["Unruly shapes but he cares not","He balances the blade","In these unwilling shapes must lie","The beauty of his trade"]],["s",148,["Do not ask him to persuade","That is not how he is made"]],["h",2,"The Young Nobleman","the-young-nobleman",0],["s",150,["Father said, one day this will all be mine","And when it comes, to leave my games behind","I have ’til then to learn to treat it well","To make the most of every hill and dell","Protect the folk who cultivate the land","Living safe is the least they will demand"]],["s",156,["All I ask is a tithe in return","They will default because some house has burned","They’ll blame the storm, they’ve had another brat","And they must never get away with that"]],["s",160,["I think I’ll manage. Then he drained his glass","A toast to plagues, he said, they too shall pass"]],["h",2,"The Bard","the-bard",0],["s",162,["Mirrored by the minstrels | the morning sun rises","Shattering the shadows | shunned by the dark","A town so sorely tired | wakes to trembling dawn","The weakness of the weary | is wiped off by a breeze","Cold but yet a comfort | crisp the morning air","A hint of rising heat | holding fog at bay","In light of daybreak living | lies the human heart","There is hope for healing | however hard it is"]],["h",2,"The Jester","the-jester",0],["s",170,["My wit provides a king’s absolution","From thinking stars revolve around the Earth","My smiling face hides the dissolution","Of all his might inherited at birth","In the truth lie seeds of revolution","The mask it wears, the silly hats of mirth","I whisper you are mortal in his ear","The mocking slave who wields the jester’s tear"]],["h",2,"The Wizard","the-wizard",0],["s",178,["There is a wizard in the woods","A man who conjures flames","The ruler over life and death","At least that’s what he claims"]],["s",182,["You must have seen him at some point","His cloak looks like a dress","He came to town before its walls","At least that’s what he says"]],["s",186,["You know the weather varies here","It changes at his word","He drained the creek, he talks to crows","At least that’s what I’ve heard"]],["s",190,["The people here don’t mention him","They don’t go to his glade","For good or ill he’s left alone","I think they’re just afraid"]],["s",194,["But still it’s best you stay away","Or find out to your loss","What he can do—for he is strange","Don’t ever make him cross"]],["h",1,"THE FIRE","the-fire",0],["h",2,"The Arc of Othering","the-arc-of-othering",0],["h",3,"Act I – The Wedding","act-i-the-wedding",0],["s",198,["Outside the church she took him by the arm","The bride was dressed in white and silver pearls","About to wed her groom—he owns a farm—","Inside were handsome men and pretty girls","The blacksmith’s youngest daughter, and the Earl’s","They talked and laughed, and crowded to their seat","A friendly nod to anyone they’d meet"]],["s",205,["The mother, who had made her daughter’s hair","Beside the father, he put up the cost","The uncles, aunts and cousins—all were there","The flowerer, so worried by the frost","The lass who hugged the puppy that got lost","A congregation filled with joy and pride","They craned their necks to welcome in the bride"]],["s",212,["Just in time! a loud voice said from behind","It hushed the crowd, from somewhere in the shade","I know that voice, I thought he had declined","The father said, why ever leave your glade","The man walked, with some noise, through the arcade","With huffs and puffs he sat down at front row","That’s my niece! he said, with that arse in tow"]],["s",219,["Despite the music, heavy silence fell","Uneasiness so quickly reignited","I think he must have heard the peel of bells","I’m sure he’s never properly invited","He seems to be the only one delighted","Though every face was turned towards the bride","Their eyes were cold and hit him like a tide"]],["s",226,["The wedding, clearly tainted by the man,","Had lost its edge of merriment and joy","It failed its promise from how it began","As everyone somehow would leave annoyed","It’s ruined for the groom, I say, poor boy","Though never certain what he did so wrong","They all were sure that he did not belong"]],["h",3,"Act II – The Merchant’s Resentment","act-ii-the-merchant-s-resentment",0],["s",233,["Let’s speak the truth—this letter came from you","It bears the Merchant’s mark to write things down","The weaver, or the dyer—or the Earl","Not one of them would ever use a pen"]],["s",237,["The worried Merchant tried to intervene","The Priest put up his palms to calm him down","You mustn’t worry—they will never know","This nameless accusation has no face"]],["s",241,["It took a righteous citizen to write","But still without an author, sent by all","So rest at ease, and leave the task to me","To light the spark—then fear will do the rest"]],["s",245,["It’s true, you know, the Bishop told me so","A ruined seed might look like it’s just fine","But trust your heart to know where there’s decay","Protect your crop from any rot within"]],["s",249,["A fiery sermon, that will do the trick","They only need an enemy within","They’re peasants, and they fear those at the top","We’ll point them to the very lowest rung"]],["s",253,["I guess that you know best, the Merchant said","The letter could perhaps have come from me","It’s true the state of things does bother me","I feel control is slipping from our hands"]],["s",257,["I’m fairly sure that he is at the root","He spreads unease wherever he would go","But what I feel inside my heart of hearts","Is dread for taking action—and for not"]],["s",261,["The Priest agreed in silence with a nod","Then smiled and whispered—Put your trust in God."]],["h",3,"Act III – The Guild Hall","act-iii-the-guild-hall",0],["s",263,["Your ear, good sirs and brothers in the Guild","I stand here full of joy, yet unfulfilled","Though proud that you have chosen me again","To be your guide—it must not be in vain","On me does fall the task to speak out loud;","Our vigilance has slept to make us cowed","Onto this threat I find it quite absurd;","That we have not yet made our voices heard"]],["s",271,["The Blacksmith rose—You speak the truth","I feel it in my blood","The dykes of change are giving way","Beware the coming flood","The Scribe said Aye, you speak for me","Our ways have seen their day","If we don’t speak, and act, as one","To hold the threat at bay"]],["s",279,["The Blacksmith waved his massive fist","We all know who’s to blame","His challenges are dangerous","Yet we speak not—for shame!"]],["s",283,["The Healer rose and cleared his throat","I deeply disagree","The vulnerable are not to blame","That much is clear to me"]],["s",287,["You see, his ways, such lack of grace","Will signify a mind","Without control—a weakened soul","Already left behind"]],["s",291,["The room erupted with protests","With challenges and jeers","A violent cackle of dispute","A tumult of their fears"]],["s",295,["By tables stained by beer and sweat","By fire-light and smoke","For long, the guildsmen disagreed","The Priest then coughed and spoke:"]],["s",299,["It is a stony path to challenge God","His church and his establishment on Earth","Yet we are all but human, we are flawed","We know what’s right but still choose joy and mirth","Temptations, all through life, we face at birth","The scripture say the guilty must be quelled","As he sat down a heavy silence fell"]],["s",306,["The Merchant slowly rose and broke the spell","We need to make a choice, and make it well","A challenge, any challenge to the Guild","From anyone, deliberate and willed"]],["s",310,["Will leave them unacknowledged—so defined","All brothers here, are we thus of one mind?","The Priest said That is where you need to go","It has the Bishop’s seal. Let it be so."]],["h",3,"Act IV – The Song of the Unseen","act-iv-the-song-of-the-unseen",0],["s",314,["There are no words in my head","That leave traces from my tongue"]],["s",316,["There is the noise—","Yes, there is that","But no words"]],["s",319,["What they hear is the echoes","But they’re not here;","Neither here nor there"]],["s",322,["The echoes escape, bounce back","From naked walls","In empty rooms—","They find their way back","Into my head"]],["s",327,["New noise. Louder.","But no words","Louder echoes. Sharper noise."]],["s",330,["The empty rooms can do nothing"]],["s",331,["There are no words in my head"]],["h",2,"The North Wind by the Tail","the-north-wind-by-the-tail",0],["h",3,"Prologue – The Jester speaks","prologue-the-jester-speaks",0],["s",332,["It takes a fool to tell a tale like ours","To whisper truths we must not disregard","A town there was, complete with walls and towers","So strong and proud yet only a façade","Come learn to see the limit of their power","Pray silence for the fool, the roguish bard","A tale of wit and jest in slanted rhyme","How truth is shaped, a story old as time"]],["h",3,"Act I – The Loss","act-i-the-loss",0],["s",340,["The clouds sped by and threatened rain","When Guilda woke and yawned","Her husband lay there fast asleep","Another day had dawned"]],["s",344,["Her husband snored with open mouth","She watched him as he slept","Dream on, she said, sweet love of mine","She thought she might have wept"]],["s",348,["No luck like hers, though honour-bound","By vows of newly-weds","The only thing I need, she thought,","My husband in my bed"]],["s",352,["She turned the handle to go out","The wind, both strong and cold","Took hold and heaved at Guilda’s door","And ripped it from her hold","It slammed against the wall and woke","Her husband from his rest","The storm came faster than I thought","He hurried to get dressed"]],["s",360,["I’ll check our friends, he said, but you","Had better stay inside","You mustn’t leave while I’m away","You’re precious, you’re my bride"]],["s",364,["The briefest kiss and then goodbye","A word and he was gone","Apart from gales for company","She was all alone"]],["s",368,["The wait was long, from day to night","She only had her will","To see her through and keep her sane","The storm will drink its fill"]],["s",372,["The fear","The thought of him without me","I must not interfere","But if he cares about me","He’d know I need him here"]],["s",377,["As morning broke the storm died down","The fear, the growing doubt","She brought her shawl to keep her warm","And ventured to go out"]],["s",381,["How brief the beats of human hearts","She heard a gentle knock","An open door, a friendly face","This will come as a shock"]],["s",385,["Her neighbour’s voice—Alas I bring","The news that we all dread","This night he saved us all, but one;","I’m sorry—but he’s dead"]],["s",389,["It was the storm that took his life","But Guilda wouldn’t hear","Nor would she see, but in her mind","The devil danced and jeered"]],["s",393,["A sudden flame within her soul","No tears came to her eye","A blend of rage and hate that burned","How comes it I don’t cry"]],["s",397,["Please tell me how he died, she said","I must know if I may","A string of words, just one sang out","The storm it was, you say?"]],["s",401,["Oh aye, the storm, a falling tree","That is the how and why","Then Guilda said, in icy voice","If so, the wind must die"]],["s",405,["It did, you know, the sky is clear","Her neighbour shook her head","But Guilda said; I’ll find its source","And then the wind is dead","Her neighbour fled when she could see","The rage in Guilda’s eyes","But Guilda closed her door and vowed","That’s how the North Wind dies"]],["h",3,"Interlude – The Jester speaks","interlude-the-jester-speaks",0],["s",413,["He is gone","He is dead","Dust is settling on his bed"]],["s",416,["That’s on him","To be fair","Maybe next time you’ll prepare"]],["s",419,["Can’t you see","Through your pain","Your revenge will be in vain"]],["h",3,"Act II – The Search","act-ii-the-search",0],["s",422,["It’s true they said, she seeks revenge","For losing what she had","The wind must pay for causing pain","They said she must be mad"]],["s",426,["But some said well, it is not fair","The storm should strike her so","If she will leave to kill the wind","Then I say let her go"]],["s",430,["So, some were for and some against","You cannot catch the sun","The shouts were loud what she should do","Some said it can’t be done"]],["s",434,["And then again, a very few","A handful—one, or two","Who said if she seeks my advice","This is not up to you"]],["s",438,["If you sing someone else’s song","You’ll end up lost, forlorn","But many sneered and egged her on","We’ve had it with the storm"]],["s",442,["So off she went to seek advice","On how to find the gale","Convince a friend to sympathise","And point her to the trail"]],["h",4,"1 – The Healer","1-the-healer",0],["s",446,["Help me, healer, Guilda pleaded","Put my soul at ease","They say you know the wind’s abode","I need it to find peace"]],["p",[["To that I must say no, alas, you see",1]],1],["p",[["There is no way to win against the wind",1]],1],["p",[["And even if in eager search you found",1]],1],["p",[["What prize would you then pay for having won?",1]],1],["p",[["Do not wallow in your wrath at the wind",1]],1],["p",[["You can’t contain it, you can ’but endure ",1]],1],["p",[["You mustn’t mourn your man with raging heart",1]],1],["p",[["The healing you would have comes not from hate",1]],1],["p",[["What mends a fevered mind is father time",1]],1],["p",[["So put your faith in patience, Guilda please",1]],1],["p",[["You asked for my advice; you must adapt",1]],1],["p",[["In quests for vengeance I will not take part",1]],1],["p",[["So speak I, as a healer, from the heart",1]],1],["s",450,["Then Guilda shrugged, I disagree","Your voice is ’but a bleat","I’d rather seek the blacksmith’s forge","The fire and the heat"]],["h",4,"2 – The Blacksmith","2-the-blacksmith",0],["s",454,["I seek you as a guide, blacksmith","The healer failed me so","My deepest wish to find the wind","So tell me where to go"]],["p",[["I heard the talk, the blacksmith said",1]],1],["p",[["The North Wind has to die",1]],1],["p",[["It seems to me they all agree",1]],1],["p",[["But noone told me why",1]],1],["p",[["It’s natural that they should not",1]],1],["p",[["Have come to me before",1]],1],["p",[["To craft the world to your design",1]],1],["p",[["You do not ask wherefore",1]],1],["p",[["You act, you strike, or open up",1]],1],["p",[["Yourself to further blows",1]],1],["p",[["He shrugged and said If I were you",1]],1],["p",[["I’d climb to find the snow",1]],1],["p",[["You find the East Wind in the plains",1]],1],["p",[["The West Wind by the sea ",1]],1],["p",[["The South Wind comes from warmer lands",1]],1],["p",[["That much is clear to me",1]],1],["p",[["The North Wind is a different beast",1]],1],["p",[["Its breath is crisp and cold",1]],1],["p",[["So climb then to the mountain’s peak",1]],1],["p",[["To find your pot of gold",1]],1],["p",[["Don’t ask, once there, what you should do",1]],1],["p",[["To kill brings no escape",1]],1],["p",[["A blacksmith does not finish life",1]],1],["p",[["He only acts to shape",1]],1],["s",458,["I’m grateful to you, blacksmith","Said Guilda, you’ve been kind","But now to learn the art of death","A soldier I must find"]],["h",4,"3 – The Young Nobleman","3-the-young-nobleman",0],["s",462,["My Lord, if you could spare me time","Said Guilda with a courtesy","I need your strength and some advice","Before I start my journey"]],["p",[["The Nobleman said what you aim to do",1]],1],["p",[["Is just and fair, and strength will see you through",1]],1],["p",[["No matter what you’re taught, what you believe",1]],1],["p",[["You must avenge the blows that you receive",1]],1],["p",[["Your pride will show you how to prove your worth",1]],1],["p",[["Establish your dominion here on Earth",1]],1],["p",[["Now learn which way to go to find your foe",1]],1],["p",[["Climb through the pass with everlasting snow",1]],1],["p",[["Bear right towards the peak and you will see",1]],1],["p",[["The faceless wind come charging down on thee",1]],1],["p",[["Now, if your heart is true you will not stop",1]],1],["p",[["Your burning rage must bring you to the top",1]],1],["p",[["That is his ancient home, he lives there still",1]],1],["p",[["The cold North Wind, the one that you must kill",1]],1],["s",466,["I thank you sir, the final ask","I have, if you’ll allow","I find the wind, we’re face to face","To kill him—Tell me how"]],["p",[["Enough of this, my patience stretches thin",1]],1],["p",[["If you are true you’ll know you must begin",1]],1],["p",[["Your weapon could be prayers to the Lord",1]],1],["p",[["But better yet, I counsel—bring a sword",1]],1],["h",3,"Interlude – The Jester speaks","interlude-the-jester-speaks-2",0],["s",470,["So off she went, the woman poor and brave","Who never once saw violence or strife","To send the wind—THE WIND—into its grave","She had no sword but brought her kitchen-knife","Don’t ever bring a fish-knife to a fight","The folly, as if blinded to the core","I try, but I can’t mock her anymore"]],["h",3,"Act III – The Wandering Wind","act-iii-the-wandering-wind",0],["h",4,"1 – Guilda’s Reflections","1-guilda-s-reflections",0],["s",477,["Though you might be as awed as you have been","Be brave, so brave, when Guilda you must go","This will not fail, your knife is small but keen","You must persist to plow on through the snow","It’s thanks to you the North Wind will not blow","Her husband’s voice she heard inside her head","But which of us, she thought, is really dead"]],["s",484,["My hold onto the world is getting thin","Should I have pushed my rage down deep and wept","How to dislodge the danger that I’m in","Can I have heard my husband though he slept","Can I turn back before my oath is kept","I’d rather die while trying to perform","The deed I crave—To kill the bloody storm"]],["h",4,"2 – The Confrontation","2-the-confrontation",0],["s",491,["The climb was steep, in truth too hard for me","Yet here I am, my vengeance has begun","The final act, when steel and wind are one","This peak of fate is now the place to be"]],["s",495,["I face my foe at last to do the deed","Today you look your last upon the sun","That is the prize you pay for what you’ve done","Eye for an eye is what will set me free"]],["p",[["The wind replied—I came to you that night",1]],1],["p",[["But you must see I don’t care what you need",1]],1],["p",[["What gives you joy or takes your pain away",1]],1],["p",[["I cannot care who flees and who would fight",1]],1],["p",[["I have no thoughts about you if you bleed",1]],1],["p",[["I see you not, you are not even prey",1]],1],["p",[["Stand down—I do not care if you agree",1]],1],["s",499,["But no","She said in shock, at last","You do care where we go","You’ve hurt us in the past","You just don’t want us to know"]],["p",[["The wind said Oh, that knife that you hold, still",1]],1],["p",[["You know it couldn’t run a paper through",1]],1],["p",[["It’s of absolutely no use to you",1]],1],["p",[["And what is more, I’m very hard to kill",1]],1],["p",[["I’ll tell you what—let’s get down off this hill",1]],1],["p",[["I’ll let you join and be the North Wind too",1]],1],["p",[["You’re not the first, I don’t know if you knew",1]],1],["p",[["The choice is yours—come join me if you will",1]],1],["s",504,["And Guilda saw her folly then, at last","To kill the wind for being what it is","Then blame the sun for rising every day","She grabbed the tail and tried to hold on fast","A thought took hold—how it had come to this","Before she was aware they were away"]],["h",4,"3 – The Flight","3-the-flight",0],["s",510,["I am the wind","I am the sky","And suddenly very much alive"]],["s",513,["To be dead","To be alive","Embrace the dream that I will fly"]],["s",516,["On the wings of the wind","Truly on its tail","The gale will drink its fill"]],["s",519,["The rush of air","The speed of sight","To be the rustle in my hair"]],["s",522,["It is the only way","I do confess","The wind’s caress"]],["s",525,["If you cannot beat it","There is the choice to be it","The storm and the flight","Shattering the night"]],["s",529,["There is no prey","There is no me","I cannot leave, nor stay","I can only BE"]],["h",3,"Epilogue – The Jester speaks","epilogue-the-jester-speaks",0],["s",533,["So there it is, the Jester says with glee","Our Guilda has become what she detests","Forever locked—or maybe she is free—","To ride the tail, to storm and to forget"]],["s",537,["If you would hunt the wind, I do foresee","You will resist advice and even threats","By then your only option is to choose","To be your foe, or fight him—and to lose"]],["s",541,["The Jester puts away his lute","He’s lost for words somehow","The faintest smile—Before he leaves","He takes a final bow"]],["h",2,"The Bride and the King","the-bride-and-the-king",0],["h",3,"Act I – Humble beginnings","act-i-humble-beginnings",0],["s",545,["The straw was soft for the lass, a simple soldier’s daughter","Destined for dreary days and hopeless dreams—and forever a maid"]],["s",547,["Every chore much the same, cheerless in the shadow of the crown","Saved by the love for the lady she served, with moments secretly shared"]],["s",549,["Above your state","Life is never simple at court","Surrounded by ambition and hate","Such positions are dearly bought","Envy has the patience to wait"]],["h",3,"Act II – An ominous decision","act-ii-an-ominous-decision",0],["s",554,["Quietly cloaking a queen, the apron of the adolescent girl","Realising regal attraction, reluctance came always too late"]],["s",556,["Ever eager to serve, awkwardly aware of danger","Silently accepting her fate, seeking her solace in vain"]],["s",558,["So one day","Knowing she must trust her chances","A momentous decision to take","To face derision, whispers and glances","The fate of the unworthy—or to go away"]],["h",3,"Act III – The secret rise","act-iii-the-secret-rise",0],["s",563,["No wedding-bells before the vows, no guests for the wary couple","No announcement, no regal reception—yet she reasoned that all of them knew"]],["s",565,["Echoes of gossip as a constant companion—glares and calls in empty halls that now were hers","Tired of trying to hide the affair, kingly insanity quickly declared"]],["s",567,["What now?","This time he has clearly gone mad, he’s insane","He has MARRIED the cow?","It told you. I knew it! Surely, she is to blame","They both must go—the question is how"]],["h",3,"Act IV – The public fall","act-iv-the-public-fall",0],["s",572,["Crowned in a church, with cheering crowds amassed","Swept away by adulation and all that she could ask for"]],["s",574,["The wave that rudely wiped away her ambitions and dreams","Brought to her—and to him—by brothers once beloved"]],["s",576,["Slammed shut","The door on their bedroom cell","A dream-thread brutally cut","Here, let them dwell","The mad-dog king and his slut"]],["h",3,"Act V – The long years","act-v-the-long-years",0],["s",581,["The dangerous phantom is finished—the fever at court reached its pitch","She dared not discuss her fate, despite that dreadful decision"]],["s",583,["Once she pondered the punishment of leaving, a prelude to a costume not her own","Now, she saw it as a welcome—a soft mask woven to wear with honour"]],["s",585,["So away","Slowly across the sea to over yonder","This time, she decided to stay","For a life of rest, and to ponder","That the maid once was a queen—for less than ninety days"]],["h",2,"The Pilgrim","the-pilgrim",0],["h",3,"Act I – Departure","act-i-departure",0],["s",590,["The Lord is my shepherd, I shall not want,","The Pilgrim said aloud and turned away","From everything she knew at Rue du Pont","And from the thought that she would rather stay","What lay ahead she knew not, but she prayed","Please let me come home safely from this quest","The glory be to you—then let me rest"]],["s",597,["A leg of lamb and two small loaves of bread","With anxious heart into a great unknown","There’s nothing for it but to go ahead","There’ll come a day they’ll say How you have grown","From what you learned and did—a girl, alone","It was not I, but God, here at my side","I trust in him; I’ll live—or I might die"]],["h",3,"Act II – The Struggle and the Fall","act-ii-the-struggle-and-the-fall",0],["s",604,["The road was long, for sleeping in the wild","She’d find a barn or a verderer’s hut","Asking for lodging, treated like a child","They all said no, with an if or a but","Blow after blow, in the pit of her gut","At last the shore, much later than she planned,","Where every ship rejected her offhand"]],["s",611,["Frustrated by the scoffs she searched in vain","When suddenly a man stood by her side","I’d like to help—you need it, that is plain","The ship I sail will not have you denied","She paid, relieved, and let him be her guide","Now hop aboard, he said and walked away","There was no fare, to him she was ’but prey"]],["h",3,"Act III – Emergence","act-iii-emergence",0],["s",618,["So deeply stranded in the town, and lost","A lonely pilgrim, tired and forlorn","A child that must be saved at any cost","So many lives, and all they know is scorn","If we should die, she thought, then who would mourn?","She kneeled by one and said I’m hungry too","Do you want help? Let’s see what we can do"]],["s",625,["The tavern’s lights were bright as they walked in","She meant to spend her last—this child must eat","But there, the thief; at dice and drinking gin","She snatched his dagger from behind his seat","He felt its point while getting on his feet","She took his purse but cut one coin in two","I’ll keep the knife so that belongs to you"]],["h",3,"Act IV – Realisation","act-iv-realisation",0],["s",632,["A voice in her head said what have you done?","A likely future, echoes from her past","To take her fate into her hands and run","When thinking of that choice, she stopped and gasped","And then sped on, towards the quay at last","She chose a ship, the child clutched to her breast","A pilgrim pair, so far from being blessed"]],["s",639,["Hands down, the sailor laughed, that is so good","Easily the funniest tale I’ve heard","You took your money back because you could","But wondered if you should—that’s too absurd","One mustn’t treat you like a fool, my word!","You saved a child while at the edge of life",[["Not only that, you also ",0],["bought ",1],["his knife!",0]]]],["h",3,"Act V – Arrival","act-v-arrival",0],["s",646,["Tell me Pilgrim, what do we do now?","The child beside her, peering at the shore","You’re strong and kind, there is wisdom on your brow","We will get by, the fear I had before","Is gone by you, I doubt not anymore","The Pilgrim nodded—yes, my child, it’s true","We’ve come this far, we’ve made it—me and you"]],["s",653,["And so it was, before she saw the church","She knew that she had reached her journey’s end","There was no further need for any search","Noone but her on who she must depend","That all the blessings looked-for were pretend","Standing on the prow with wind in her hair","Almost within touch of Bælwythe, the fair"]],["h",2,"The Fire and the Crown","the-fire-and-the-crown",0],["h",3,"Act I – A Dagger in the Dark","act-i-a-dagger-in-the-dark",0],["s",660,["You almost see a shadow move","Beyond your edge of sight","I touch my blade, so keen and sharp","And black against the night"]],["s",664,["I drop a leaflet by your door","Your friends will never know","If you decide to read it, or","You’d rather let it go"]],["s",668,["Truth is revolutionary","You know this, deep inside","It’s up to you to stand and fight","Or choose to bow and hide"]],["s",672,["Come join us now, a brave new world","Is waiting in the wing","Let truth be told, both wide and loud","Let’s make the people sing"]],["s",676,["But not just yet, await the sign","Do not shout out too soon","Let freedom boom, but stealthily","On nights without a moon"]],["s",680,["My Liege, my Lord–we play pretend","The fire that we bring","Will light one day, with bells, and they","Will fear how freedom rings"]],["h",3,"Act II – The Ruler","act-ii-the-ruler",0],["s",684,["I cannot tell him what to do, only what to think","I do not like it more than you do, I think it stinks","The Jester sighed and shook his head","You must keep them fed, and safe, and—things","You will personally pay for what the future brings","If I did more than plant his thoughts then surely I’d be dead"]],["s",690,["The Chamberlain stared back and snapped","Do you really think I’m not aware of that?","I have the vanity of a king to quell","Let him hunt and dance and pretend to rule","If he needs to prance around and play the fool","While the people in the streets quietly rebel"]],["s",696,["I’m not surprised, there’s not enough to eat","The Jester said, and everyone you meet","Has the light of revolution in their eyes","Should they catch you as a liar","It might spark their raging fire","Rest assured, it won’t be just the King that dies"]],["s",702,["Do be quiet, a fool knows nothing, the Chamberlain replied","The women of the land have ever cried","Of famine and of the children they must feed","There is no food in a revolution","Deep down, they want us to supply the resolution","And stability is everything they need"]],["s",708,["The Jester frowned and said I’m not so sure","We’ve been in this situation before","This strategy of yours to keep the king in the dark","Come dawn, the people will eat the bitter flour that you milled","I can picture now the barricades they’ll build","Remember, this kindling only needs the smallest spark"]],["h",3,"Act III – The Court","act-iii-the-court",0],["s",714,["The King said you must tell me what to do","You’re scared, I know, and wish to hide away","The throne and crown do not belong to you","You’d better bring your sharpest anyway"]],["s",718,["I hear the sound of singing in the street","The sky vibrates with anger and with hate","I smell the smoke and hear the marching feet","So is the day then here to seal my fate?"]],["s",722,["The Chamberlain said, no my Lord, not yet","There’s still the holy Mother Church to use","To teach them what they give is what they get","That’s how a revolution is defused"]],["s",726,["Of course, the King said, celebrate their strife","We’ll let the bishops preach on after-life"]],["h",3,"Act IV – The Spark","act-iv-the-spark",0],["s",728,["The spark was lit, there was no turning back","A word, a push in a crowded alley","The swift retaliatory attack","The fire raged from village to valley","And even as the word had spread in court","The Chamberlain advised the King to flee","To go, to use this very last resort","Such a noble plea—Leave the key with me"]],["s",736,["So I’m dead, said the Bishop to the Priest","They think the cross can stop a violent mob","Then I should be the fodder for the beast","Indeed a way of learning on the job"]],["s",740,["So as the King rode away across the downs","His Bishop sacrifice headed into town"]],["h",3,"The Aftermath – The Jester speaks","the-aftermath-the-jester-speaks",0],["s",742,["The King has fled, the Bishop’s dead","The Chamberlain has lost","The message sent has torn a rent","As mothers count the cost"]],["s",746,["For so it is—you hit, you miss","And lose your only child","Though dead he be, don’t look to me","The Jester can’t be riled"]],["s",750,["My clinging bells—the screams and yells","Are all in minor key","We lose, we win, I wear my grin","The truth will set us free"]],["h",3,"Epilogue","epilogue",0],["s",754,["Truth ever has a cost—","for the honest as for the liar—","but still we sing,","because we must,","because we are human"]],["h",2,"The Healer’s Mistake","the-healer-s-mistake",0],["s",759,["This cracks me up, the Jester said","That holier-than-thou","Demeanour that she radiates","A real self-righteous cow"]],["s",763,["With such a stiff-necked attitude","You’d think she knows her way","Around the human body-parts","And name them any day"]],["s",767,["Well, this one seems to be less smart","Than others of her trade","You might wonder however she","Received the passing grade"]],["s",771,["A simple operation then","Can be beyond her skill","To lie beneath that knife of hers","Yes, risk that, you who will"]],["s",775,["The tendon that she fixed last week","Quickly comes to mind","She put things back where they should be","But one piece left behind"]],["s",779,["That’s strange she said, what is that thing","I don’t know where it goes","Let’s hope he doesn’t use it much","He wouldn’t, I suppose"]],["s",783,["The lesson here—you shouldn’t go","To Healers with degree","From Common Sense Academy","If it were up to me"]],["h",2,"The Archbishop and the King","the-archbishop-and-the-king",0],["s",787,["We would offer you some beer, dear Bishop","The King held out his hand to have it kissed","Though bread and water likely suits you better"]],["s",790,["I thank you, no, my Lord, but watered wine","Just half a glass to wash the dust away","I have to say the journey here was hot","The aging bishop slowly wiped his brow"]],["s",794,["A gesture from the King, the wine was served","Now then, he said, just what is this we hear","A monastery that defies its bishop","Do you allow your monks to mock you, too?"]],["s",798,["The Bishop blushed but hid away his anger","My monks will follow rules set by the saint"]],["s",800,["The King replied; That is not what we are hearing","The issue here is politics—and you","You clearly let your monks make plays for power"]],["s",803,["My Lord, they pray. They worship and they sing","At heart, they long for silent contemplation","They only wish to save your soul for heaven"]],["s",806,["So why do they keep begging for donations?","Our people pay, and you just meditate"]],["s",808,["The Bishop humbly bowed his head and smiled","That is the role of holy mother church","Our worship needs the finest you can give","That’s horse-shit, Priest, and very well you know it","They make you rich, your humbug rituals","And now this John of yours, this upstart prior","We asked him as politely as we can","To do his King a small yet vital service","He had the bloody nerve to turn us down"]],["s",817,["Well yes, my Lord, for him there was no choice","I take it this concerns your servant’s daughter?"]],["s",819,["My Chamberlain is hardly someone’s servant","But yes, it does—a worthy man, and loyal","His daughter is as sharp as any blade","And she would do your monastery proud"]],["s",823,["Well, Lord King, the notion that a prior","Should take a woman on if but to teach","The Bishop shrugged and let his silence fall"]],["s",826,["With rising wrath the King persisted","So must we frame this as a king’s command?"]],["s",828,["Perhaps you might refrain, it’s not our custom","The task is plain—to save immortal souls","Authority is given to the Church","There will not be a substitute for greatness","The finest mind will always be a man"]],["s",833,["A heavy silence settled on the room","The King then pointed straight toward the Bishop","You hypocritical, righteous lackwit","You save immortal souls, or so you claim","We offer you a soul as pure as dewdrops","And yet you say that she’s not good enough","The Bishop stood his ground and tried again","May I suggest the Chamberlain has motives","Which may not be to save his daughter’s soul,","Perhaps to set her up for royal office?"]],["s",843,["If so, that should not matter to a priest","You would do well to keep in mind what’s yours","And, even more important—what is ours","But come, old friend, let’s keep this council friendly","What can we give you, what is it you need?","For surely, there are comforts that you lack"]],["s",849,["Your Majesty, to that I must not yield","For if I did—what would the angels say","How would I see myself in the looking-glass","If I had chosen wealth before the word"]],["s",853,["Then so be it, the King said in a whisper","Your grab for power leaves us with no choice","We cannot let the Church be independent","Its wealth goes back into the royal coffers","And from now on, you answer but to us"]],["s",858,["The Bishop gasped—You know not what you’re doing","These plans of yours are welcomed by the Devil","Are you so bold to gamble with your soul?"]],["s",861,["The King turned cold with murder in his eyes","I’ll see you hang for that, bishop though you be","With luck, you have a moment left to flee"]],["s",864,["Behind the King, relaxing on the table","The Jester strokes his lute and starts to sing","If you be holy or if you be royal","If you were born by wealthy or by poor","I do believe control is so important","To you that nothing will stand in your way","I see you grabbing on to it so dearly","Ignoring the illusion that it is","You did not ever have it in your keeping","And once you see that, now you never will"]],["h",2,"The Debate","the-debate",0],["s",874,["The older monk refused to bow","A heretic, you say?","My voice is raised to please the Lord","I do not think I stray"]],["s",878,["The monk in brown then crossed his arms","Do not presume to know","Your habit is as black as sin","Appropriately so"]],["s",882,["Your claim that reason strengthens faith","And seek to understand","The holy Father thus has ruled","That view of yours is banned"]],["s",886,["The truth is one—and only one","There is no need to search","We praise the Lord by faith and prayer","And reach him through the church"]],["s",890,["The monk in black said Hear me out","My faith is thus maintained","When seeing winter turn to spring","If leaves could be explained"]],["s",894,["The younger monk, in brown, said no","Your words come out uncouth","For man must never overturn","The unity of truth"]],["s",898,["Our minds are not infallible","As is the word revealed","The scripture has the final truth","It has our Father’s seal"]],["s",902,["The older monk said Tell me this;","In many aged brow","Of monks in black and monks in brown","But age will not allow"]],["s",906,["These monks to deepen thoughts and prayer","Their eye-sight is too poor","To read the words that God has sent","As they could do before"]],["s",910,["But Praise the Lord! for someone did","Apply their reason thus","Inventing glasses for their eyes","Is that then treasonous?"]],["s",914,["You, too, would treasure useful things","I’m sure it cannot be","A crime against the word of God","To help a monk to see"]],["s",918,["Idolatry and blasphemy","The younger monk proclaimed","The older monk, defiantly","Said then I’d stand ashamed"]],["s",922,["Fides quaerens intellectum","The mind you must acquit","But finger raised, the younger monk","Said Anathema sit."]],["h",2,"The Bard and the Jester","the-bard-and-the-jester",0],["s",926,["I see the quiet dignity of man","How each of us will try and fail and fall","Yet every one of us since we began","In secret wields the will to heed the call","To live and love whatever might befall","Though often beaten down upon one knee","The human soul will rise, for it is free"]],["s",933,["The Bard thus sang of beauty with a smile","While Jester speaks the truth but with a frown","I see you think their spirit is worthwhile","It’s true that men get up when they fall down","They swim because they do not wish to drown","Oh Jester, said the Bard, you must be blind","They swim for they are part of humankind"]],["h",2,"The Healing of Bælwythe","the-healing-of-baelwythe",0],["h",3,"Act 1 : Disaster","act-1-disaster",0],["s",940,["The Guild had worked for thirteen weeks","Extending on their hall","They long had needed somewhere safe—","A space to fit them all"]],["s",944,["The sudden storm had turned to gale","and shifted to the west","Before the guild got out of bed","With some not even dressed"]],["s",948,["In groups of twos and threes they stood","Uncertain and in fear","In shrieks and roar from violent winds","They heard the devil jeer"]],["s",952,["Then feeble efforts of a few","To break the passive spell","The fire in the hearth still hot","And resin burns too well"]],["s",956,["Midnight saw the tiles blow off","The scaffolds were no more","At early light the roof fell in","And with it, walls and floor"]],["s",960,["When finished with its task at last","The wind died with the night","The sun shone over labour lost","Ironically bright"]],["s",964,["The town was there in force, alone","To watch the Guild-hall burn","In heavy silence noone spoke","And every eye would turn"]],["s",968,["What now?","The silence lingering","Where now is there to go?","The doubt provides its king","The dice will have its throw"]],["h",3,"Act 2 : Salvation","act-2-salvation",0],["s",973,["On the Sunday, three days on,","The town still smelled of smoke","The ashes still and silent now","The people barely spoke"]],["s",977,["Reluctantly they went to church","Or to be reassured","While some went out of habit, and","Expected to be bored"]],["s",981,["But none expected to be blamed","To hear the bishop say","Disasters lay at Bælwythe’s feet","Get on your knees and pray!"]],["s",985,["To utter silence he pronounced","His doom, as preachers do,","That God has sent this violent storm","As punishment of you"]],["s",989,["Of you! he roared, For lack of faith—","For shame, I see you frown","’Twas you, not I, who chose the Guild","No wonder it burnt down"]],["s",993,["’Twas not a month ago I asked,","Nay, pleaded with you all","To build the church a taller tow’r","Your choice is now your fall"]],["s",997,["Repent! Repent! It’s not too late","You still can make amends","Forgo your hall and build the church","Before this saga ends"]],["s",1001,["A taller church, a splendid cross","With lights of green and gold","’Tis what your Father asks of you","And thus your faith behold"]],["s",1005,["The congregation left the church","Later on that day","With downcast hearts and ill at ease","They knew not what to say"]],["s",1009,["Hold on!","Extend the church, he said","Is that for us to do?","If towers trump our bread","We’d better see it through"]],["h",3,"Act 3 : Giving","act-3-giving",0],["s",1014,["The blacksmiths came, the bakers too","The wheelwright and his wife","All masters and apprentices","The brewer, large as life"]],["s",1018,["Through masons’ toil and expertise","By glaziers and their skills","The slender tower slowly rose","As stable as the hills"]],["s",1022,["The master builder shook his head","The cladding must begin","In six weeks’ time we must be done","Before the frost sets in"]],["s",1026,["With doubled pace—to be on time","They left no stone unturned","So every other task would wait","Even the house that burned"]],["s",1030,["The monks would join the hardest tasks","To move the work along","They brought their cheese, with bread and beer","And sometimes even song"]],["s",1034,["This tithe releases us from sin","This mortar saves a soul","Repentance for our lack of faith","These stones will make us whole"]],["s",1038,["With children hungry from the lack","Of tilling of the fields","At least it’s done, they seemed to say,","Let’s see now what it yields"]],["s",1042,["I am content, the Lord is pleased","The bishop let them know","This tower you have built for God","His love for you will grow"]],["s",1046,["Let’s hope!","The church might do or don’t","And leave us still unheard","The bishop says it won’t","We only have his word"]],["h",3,"Act 4 : Revelation","act-4-revelation",0],["s",1051,["A fortnight passed, when farmers tilled","While shoes and clothes were made","As trust in life increased each day","In secret, plans were laid"]],["s",1055,["The Guild still needs a place to meet","Aye, and one that doesn’t burn!","Well, I can’t waste my time on that","Be silent, wait your turn"]],["s",1059,["Do you not see what I must face","But surely, we agree","If I cannot feed my children","Should I then work for free?"]],["s",1063,["For days, the Guild discussed their course","To wait or build again","With clouds of thunder gathering","A threat of coming rain"]],["s",1067,["Then suddenly a cry went up","The tower is on fire!","A bolt of lightning—sent by God","Had hit the tallest spire"]],["s",1071,["Debate aside, they rushed to see","Disaster strike anew","It was already much too late","The bolt had hit too true"]],["s",1075,["There was no hurry—all could see","From window, street and porch","The tower they had built for God","Was burning like a torch"]],["s",1079,["The monastery also burned","For sparks fell from the church","The cloisters, and the library","The end of much research"]],["s",1083,["So much for promises, they said","From preachers and from fools","They talk of heaven—this is hell","We should not be their tools"]],["s",1087,["The bishop, watching all alone","At last bereft of might","His face, all lit by dancing flames","Was ashen in its light"]],["s",1091,["Well then!","The gold has turned to dust","A castle in the sand","Now let them earn our trust","I say this will not stand"]],["h",3,"Act 5 : Beginnings","act-5-beginnings",0],["s",1096,["It is a trial, hear me out","Your minds are still in doubt","Your thoughts remain with gold—not God","Which you must do without"]],["s",1100,["He needs your hearts, but trusts you not","You’ve still to prove your faith","At judgement day, when you are called","Your riches have no sway"]],["s",1104,["Standing by the ruined wall","The haggard bishop spoke","With craftsmen standing idly by","The church yard wreathed in smoke"]],["s",1108,["A heavy silence, like a wall","That no words can break through","The only sound, a lonely voice—","Well, that is nothing new"]],["s",1112,["A murmur of agreement rose","We’ve heard it all before","They are ’but empty promises","Won’t listen anymore"]],["s",1116,["Then, one by one, they turned away","And left without a word","The bishop speaking for the birds","A sermon noone heard"]],["h",3,"Act 6 : Healing","act-6-healing",0],["s",1120,["The hammers beat a steady tune","On iron and on stone","The saws and axes wrought the wood","With their familiar tone"]],["s",1124,["The monastery library","Rebuilt, as good as new","The reused bricks of cloister walls","Meant refuge for the few"]],["s",1128,["The master masons and their crews","The woodwrights and the cooks","Mixed in with weather-beaten men","Were girls with bonnie looks"]],["s",1132,["At lunch there rose a tempting smell","Of onions and fish","The work was hard but full of joy","As much as one could wish"]],["s",1136,["Hold up!","Is that the Earl I see","Come riding with his men?","What’s he to you and me","He can turn ’round again"]],["s",1141,["The Earl rode in to horns’ salute","With flags and men-at-arms","He stopped amongst the working men","And hands from outer farms"]],["s",1145,["I say!, said he, This will not stand!","Your lord will have his due","This monastery’s build must wait","Until my castle’s through"]],["s",1149,["You there, mason, with your trowel","So busy as of late","You work to build a room for books","And surely that can wait"]],["s",1153,["For books, he thought, and said out loud","He couldn’t hide his scorn","Authority again let slip","The mask it’d always worn"]],["s",1157,["I work for those who work for us","And not for trumped-up laws","The mason said and walked away","He didn’t even pause"]],["s",1161,["That’s true, a passing handmaid said","They helped when we were down","The monks did, but no sign of you","When the devil was in town"]],["s",1165,["The dumbstruck Earl could only watch","As work continued on","As beams were hoisted rhythmically","The beats marked with a song"]],["s",1169,["If handmaids aren’t afraid of me","He thought and bit his lip","If all of Bælwythe joins this cause","Then power slips its grip"]],["s",1173,["He turned around to lick his wounds","Nobody watched him ride","With many horse-men in his wake","But noone by his side"]],["s",1177,["At dusk the hammers stopped their beat","On chisels that they drove","For families to gather ’round","The fire in their stove"]],["h",1,"The Jester’s Illusion","the-jester-s-illusion",0],["s",1181,["Some time ago, and far away","A golden crown was lost","A patient rise, yet quick to fall","The rhythm of the frost"]],["s",1185,["I told him so, the Jester said,","His reign would never stand","I said they’d had enough of kings","And castles in the sand"]],["s",1189,["I always thought, he said and sighed,","You earn the right to rule","It’s hard to tell if he or I","Deserves to play the fool"]]]},"fire":{"title":"Fire in Bælwythe","by":"Dan Engström","pub":"Piratpensionat Produktion","year":"2026","sub":"A monodrama in one act, adapted from the world of Hearts Around the Fire. Performed by the Jester.","about":"A one-act play for a single actor: the Jester tells the story of Bælwythe, using poems from Hearts Around the Fire.","blocks":[["h",1,"The Jester’s Illusion","the-jester-s-illusion",0],["s",0,["Some time ago, and far away","A golden crown was lost","A patient rise, yet quick to fall","The rhythm of the frost"]],["s",4,["I told him so, the Jester said,","His reign would never stand","I said they’d had enough of kings","And castles in the sand"]],["s",8,["I always thought, he said and sighed,","You earn the right to rule","It’s hard to tell if he or I","Deserves to play the fool"]],["h",1,"Directions","directions",1],["p","Dramatis personæ: ",0],["p","The Jester",0],["p","The Jester acts, mimics or impersonates the different characters as the story unfolds. He turns quickly from passion to detachment, from mocking to empathy, from roars to whispers.",0],["p","The stage is bare with black cloth as backdrop. The props are a stool and a hanger with items of clothing. As the play begins, the lights are still on in the auditorium.",0],["p","In the truth lie seeds of revolution.",0],["p","Welcome to Bælwythe. ",0],["h",1,"Scene I The Hearth","scene-i-the-hearth",0],["p",[["Enter Jester, carrying a lantern that is not lit.",1]],1],["h",2,"The Jester’s Welcome","the-jester-s-welcome",0],["s",12,["The walls that you have passed inside","And into Bælwythe fair","Will make you safe, but also blind—","It’s best you stay aware"]],["s",16,["When soon we turn the lights down low","You’ll learn what is at stake","For dignity of humankind","It’s best you stay awake"]],["s",20,["One cannot see when fast asleep—","Or even at the verge—","Prick up your ears and sit up straight","Then meaning will emerge"]],["s",24,["Enjoy this tale, this spectacle,","This play that you attend","Though be his comments sharp as nails","This Jester is your friend"]],["s",28,["So join me now—pay heed to this","A story I will tell","Of steel and stone, of war and peace","Of Bælwythe, where we dwell"]],["p",[["The lights go down in the theatre, the stage is still dimly lit. The Jester lights the lantern and puts it on the stool. The lights go slightly up on stage.",1]],1],["h",2,"The Town","the-town",0],["s",32,["Through chalky fields the river finds the sea","A man in weathered hat decides to stay","Picks up his axe and eyes the woods and bay","This river’s bend shall be a home to me"]],["s",36,["For fuel and fish, and game that’s roaming free","The builders come from near and far away","Some honest men, some sinners as they may","The fishermen tie vessels to the quay"]],["s",40,["Then rules and rulers, then the hang-man’s hill","Lurking at the edge of the village green","The church is small yet dominates the square","The hearths and homes put down at owner’s will","The refuse reek where flowers once had been","The rich prefer their houses to have stairs"]],["s",46,["So many poor","Buildings reaching higher","Make sure you bar your doors","Then famine and the fire","Songs of ruin from the choir"]],["s",51,["The streets return to life but now they're broad","Straight and paved and wide, like the plans they laid","With life renewed the cries of anguish fade","There is a bridge where once there was a ford"]],["s",55,["The boats come back with families on board","The merchants too, and makers to persuade","The blacksmith finds the tools that he had made","The builder’s hammer, and the soldier’s sword"]],["s",59,["With every step the silent tensions rise","When he is gone this land might well be mine","The builder’s tools, the sword the blacksmith found","The choice of which to wield, so say the wise","To build or to protect, to do or die","A pocket of communion makes a town"]],["h",1,"Scene II The Hearts","scene-ii-the-hearts",0],["p","This is Bælwythe, the hearth. Now sitting comfortably at the river’s bend, hugged by the hills and fields, the ruins of its walls tell a story of a dramatic, ancient past. ",0],["p","Passing its gates, walking along its alleys, I hear soft murmurs in the air. I see no one. But there are people here–and they have voices, distinct voices. Sometimes they whisper, but more often I hear them talking in small groups as they go about their daily business. They debate and argue. ",0],["p","Sometimes, there is song, or at least rhythm. The rhythm of the blacksmith’s hammer, of night and day or the rhythm of the seasons, so important for the livelihood of the people in the town. There are shouts from the market, the rights to which were dearly bought from the king when the town was little but a hamlet.",0],["p","A little while ago, I entered through the East gate on a Thursday morning. It occurred to me that I still hear echoes of the voices of the dead, soft but clear as trumpets. The whisper that they once were here. They worked and loved, and fought and failed. Only now, I hear them through the voices of the living, of my contemporaries. We are the same. We feel the same. We work and we fail, but still we carry on, as they did. We still have the need to gather around the hearth and open our hearts to one another. We still are both fire and ice. ",0],["p","They are the Hearts of Bælwythe.",0],["h",2,"The Dyer","the-dyer",0],["p","Take the Dyer for example.",0],["s",67,["I straighten out a tiny crease,","Feeling the fabric of the fleece","The touch of the palm of my hand","Takes stock of every single strand","The way it speaks and how it reads,","The cloth will tell me what it needs"]],["s",73,["An image forms inside my mind","Of soul and colour intertwined","Both earthy brown or crimson red","Sing clear to me inside my head"]],["s",77,["With each new fabric that is dyed","Each cloth transformed with worker’s pride","By all the stories they will tell","The dyer is transformed as well"]],["h",2,"The Merchant","the-merchant",0],["p","The Merchant and his hidden treasure has a different outlook to life.",0],["s",81,["The pride that fills a day of honest toil","To find fatigue fits well upon your brow","To nurture needs like farmers work the soil","Your pledge to help—the merchant’s ox and plough—","Will find your treasure while you fathom how","To grow your fortune, fail and try anew","At rest, at night, to know it’s up to you"]],["h",2,"The Brewer","the-brewer",0],["p","And then again, there is the Brewer, who sings to an altogether different tune.",0],["s",88,["In the beginning there was beer","So fine, the yield of yeast that year","Even then, before creation","The sweet scent of fermentation"]],["s",92,["He smiled and loosed the loudest laugh","Yes, that could be my epitaph","I jest with Genesis, and how","Just know that I refuse to bow","When life is hard and death is near","Nothing as holy as a beer"]],["s",98,["Peaceful, pious prayer for you, monk","I toast the courage of the drunk"]],["h",2,"The Bard","the-bard",0],["p","It seems to me that in every town, there is at least one optimistic fool, at least one silly Bard.",0],["s",100,["Mirrored by the minstrels | the morning sun rises","Shattering the shadows | shunned by the dark","A town so sorely tired | wakes to trembling dawn","The weakness of the weary | is wiped off by a breeze","Cold but yet a comfort | crisp the morning air","A hint of rising heat | holding fog at bay","In light of daybreak living | lies the human heart","There is hope for healing | however hard it is"]],["h",2,"The Jester","the-jester",0],["p","And then there is me. Your friendly voice, reminding you of what you are.",0],["s",108,["My wit provides a king’s absolution","From thinking stars revolve around the Earth","My smiling face hides the dissolution","Of all his might inherited at birth","In the truth lie seeds of revolution","The mask it wears, the silly hats of mirth","I whisper you are mortal in his ear","The mocking slave who wields the jester’s tear"]],["h",2,"The Wizard","the-wizard",0],["p","Before we take plunge into the fire, let me introduce the Wizard. Noone’s sure if he IS a wizard, but there really are a lot of stories about him. Kill a man with a look of the eye, that one.",0],["s",116,["There is a wizard in the woods","A man who conjures flames","The ruler over life and death","At least that’s what he claims"]],["s",120,["You must have seen him at some point","His cloak looks like a dress","He came to town before its walls","At least that’s what he says"]],["s",124,["You know the weather varies here","It changes at his word","He drained the creek, he talks to crows","At least that’s what I’ve heard"]],["s",128,["The people here don’t mention him","They don’t go to his glade","For good or ill he’s left alone","I think they’re just afraid"]],["s",132,["But still it’s best you stay away","Or find out to your loss","What he can do—for he is strange","Don’t ever make him cross"]],["h",1,"Scene III The Fire","scene-iii-the-fire",0],["p","There you have them – the Hearts, gathered as if around a hearth. Let’s add some fire to that hearth, shall we? Let’s see what people have to say about the Wizard.",0],["h",2,"The Arc of Othering","the-arc-of-othering",0],["h",3,"Episode I – The Wedding","episode-i-the-wedding",0],["s",136,["Outside the church she took him by the arm","The bride was dressed in white and silver pearls","About to wed her groom—he owns a farm—","Inside were handsome men and pretty girls","The blacksmith’s youngest daughter, and the Earl’s","They talked and laughed, and crowded to their seat","A friendly nod to anyone they’d meet"]],["s",143,["The mother, who had made her daughter’s hair","Beside the father, he put up the cost","The uncles, aunts and cousins—all were there","The flowerer, so worried by the frost","The lass who hugged the puppy that got lost","A congregation filled with joy and pride","They craned their necks to welcome in the bride"]],["s",150,["Just in time! a loud voice said from behind","It hushed the crowd, from somewhere in the shade","I know that voice, I thought he had declined","The father said, why ever leave your glade","The man walked, with some noise, through the arcade","With huffs and puffs he sat down at front row","That’s my niece! he said, with that arse in tow"]],["s",157,["Despite the music, heavy silence fell","Uneasiness so quickly reignited","I think he must have heard the peel of bells","I’m sure he’s never properly invited","He seems to be the only one delighted","Though every face was turned towards the bride","Their eyes were cold and hit him like a tide"]],["s",164,["The wedding, clearly tainted by the man,","Had lost its edge of merriment and joy","It failed its promise from how it began","As everyone somehow would leave annoyed","It’s ruined for the groom, I say, poor boy","Though never certain what he did so wrong","They all were sure that he did not belong"]],["h",3,"Episode II – The Merchant’s Resentment","episode-ii-the-merchant-s-resentment",0],["p","I am sure you never did that. You never had that nagging feeling of unease just because others had it. And you never, never acted on it.  Follow me down the rabbit hole of social unease.",0],["s",171,["Let’s speak the truth—this letter came from you","It bears the Merchant’s mark to write things down","The weaver, or the dyer—or the Earl","Not one of them would ever use a pen"]],["s",175,["The worried Merchant tried to intervene","The Priest put up his palms to calm him down","You mustn’t worry—they will never know","This nameless accusation has no face"]],["s",179,["It took a righteous citizen to write","But still without an author, sent by all","So rest at ease, and leave the task to me","To light the spark—then fear will do the rest"]],["s",183,["It’s true, you know, the Bishop told me so","A ruined seed might look just like it’s just fine","But trust your heart to know where there’s decay","Protect your crop from any rot within"]],["s",187,["A fiery sermon, that will do the trick","They only need an enemy within","They’re peasants, and they fear those at the top","We’ll point them to the very lowest rung"]],["s",191,["I guess that you know best, the Merchant said","The letter could perhaps have come from me","It’s true the state of things does bother me","I feel control is slipping from our hands"]],["s",195,["I’m fairly sure that he is at the root","He spreads unease wherever he would go","But what I feel inside my heart of hearts","Is dread for taking action—and for not"]],["s",199,["The Priest agreed in silence with a nod","Then smiled and whispered—Put your trust in God."]],["h",3,"Episode III – The Guild Hall","episode-iii-the-guild-hall",0],["p","We could stop here, with events set in motion—what follows is predictable, almost inevitable. Feel deep down in your heart: you know what you would do.",0],["s",201,["Your ear, good sirs and brothers in the Guild","I stand here full of joy, yet unfulfilled","Though proud that you have chosen me again","To be your guide—it must not be in vain","On me does fall the task to speak out loud;","Our vigilance has slept to make us cowed","Onto this threat I find it quite absurd;","That we have not yet made our voices heard"]],["s",209,["The Blacksmith rose—You speak the truth","I feel it in my blood","The dykes of change are giving way","Beware the coming flood"]],["s",213,["The Scribe said Aye, you speak for me","Our ways have seen their day","If we don’t speak, and act, as one","To hold the threat at bay"]],["s",217,["The Blacksmith waved his massive fist","We all know who’s to blame","His challenges are dangerous","Yet we speak not—for shame!"]],["s",221,["The Healer rose and cleared his throat","I deeply disagree","The vulnerable are not to blame","That much is clear to me"]],["s",225,["You see, his ways, such lack of grace","Will signify a mind","Without control—a weakened soul","Already left behind"]],["s",229,["The room erupted with protests","With challenges and jeers","A violent cackle of dispute","A tumult of their fears"]],["s",233,["By tables stained by beer and sweat","By fire-light and smoke","For long, the guildsmen disagreed","The Priest then coughed and spoke:"]],["s",237,["It is a stony path to challenge God","His church and his establishment on Earth","Yet we are all but human, we are flawed","We know what’s right but still choose joy and mirth","Temptations, all through life, we face at birth","The scripture says the guilty must be quelled","As he sat down a heavy silence fell"]],["s",244,["The Merchant slowly rose and broke the spell","We need to make a choice, and make it well","A challenge, any challenge to the Guild","From anyone, deliberate and willed"]],["s",248,["Will leave them unacknowledged—so defined","All brothers here, are we thus of one mind?","The Priest said That is where you need to go","It has the Bishop’s seal. Let it be so."]],["p",[["The Jester puts out the lantern, and the stage goes dark. A spotlight follows the Jester around.",1]],1],["h",3,"Episode IV – The Song of the Unseen","episode-iv-the-song-of-the-unseen",0],["p","What to do when the world fractures around you? When pushed outside, what would you do?",0],["s",252,["There are no words in my head","That leave traces from my tongue"]],["s",254,["There is the noise—","Yes, there is that","But no words"]],["s",257,["What they hear are the echoes","But they’re not here;","Neither here nor there"]],["s",260,["The echoes escape, bounce back","From naked walls","In empty rooms—","They find their way back","Into my head"]],["s",265,["New noise. Louder.","But no words","Louder echoes. Sharper noise."]],["s",268,["The empty rooms can do nothing"]],["s",269,["There are no words in my head"]],["p",[["The light on stage comes back up.",1]],1],["h",2,"The Fire and the Crown","the-fire-and-the-crown",0],["p","Yes, yes—so much for the lowest rung on the social ladder.",0],["p","Now let’s see what the highest rung is up to. We’ll make it political.",0],["p","I see shadows in the dark. Can the crown stand the heat from the fire that is to come? ",0],["h",3,"Episode I – A Dagger in the Dark","episode-i-a-dagger-in-the-dark",0],["s",271,["You almost see a shadow move","Beyond your edge of sight","I touch my blade, so keen and sharp","And black against the night"]],["s",275,["I drop a leaflet by your door","Your friends will never know","If you decide to read it, or","You’d rather let it go"]],["s",279,["Truth is revolutionary","You know this, deep inside","It’s up to you to stand and fight","Or choose to bow and hide"]],["s",283,["Come join us now, a brave new world","Is waiting in the wing","Let truth be told, both wide and loud","Let’s make the people sing"]],["s",287,["But not just yet, await the sign","Do not shout out too soon","Let freedom boom, but stealthily","On nights without a moon"]],["s",291,["My Liege, my Lord–we play pretend","The fire that we bring","Will light one day, with bells, and they","Will fear how freedom rings"]],["h",3,"Episode II – The Ruler","episode-ii-the-ruler",0],["s",295,["I cannot tell him what to do, only what to think","I do not like it more than you do, I think it stinks","The Jester sighed and shook his head","You must keep them fed, and safe, and—things","You will personally pay for what the future brings","If I did more than plant his thoughts then surely I’d be dead"]],["s",301,["The Chamberlain stared back and snapped","Do you really think I’m not aware of that?","I have the vanity of a king to quell","Let him hunt and dance and pretend to rule","If he needs to prance around and play the fool","While the people in the streets quietly rebel"]],["s",307,["I’m not surprised, there’s not enough to eat","The Jester said, and everyone you meet","Has the light of revolution in their eyes","Should they catch you as a liar","It might spark their raging fire","Rest assured, it won’t be just the King that dies"]],["s",313,["Do be quiet, a fool knows nothing, the Chamberlain replied","The women of the land have ever cried","Of famine and of the children they must feed","There is no food in a revolution","Deep down, they want us to supply the resolution","And stability is everything they need"]],["s",319,["The Jester frowned and said I’m not so sure","We’ve been in this situation before","This strategy of yours to keep the king in the dark","Come dawn, the people will eat the bitter flour that you milled","I can picture now the barricades they’ll build","Remember, this kindling only needs the smallest spark"]],["h",3,"Episode III – The Court","episode-iii-the-court",0],["s",325,["The King said you must tell me what to do","You’re scared, I know, and wish to hide away","The throne and crown do not belong to you","You’d better bring your sharpest anyway"]],["s",329,["I hear the sound of singing in the street","The sky vibrates with anger and with hate","I smell the smoke and hear the marching feet","So is the day then here to seal my fate?"]],["s",333,["The Chamberlain said, no my Lord, not yet","There’s still the holy Mother Church to use","To teach them what they give is what they get","That’s how a revolution is defused"]],["s",337,["Of course, the King said, celebrate their strife","We’ll let the bishops preach on after-life"]],["h",3,"Episode IV – The Spark","episode-iv-the-spark",0],["s",339,["The spark was lit, there was no turning back","A word, a push in a crowded alley","The swift retaliatory attack","The fire raged from village to valley"]],["s",343,["And even as the word had spread in court","The Chamberlain advised the King to flee","To go, to use this very last resort","Such a noble plea—Leave the key with me"]],["s",347,["So I’m dead, said the Bishop to the Priest","They think the cross can stop a violent mob","Then I should be the fodder for the beast","Indeed a way of learning on the job"]],["s",351,["So as the King rode away across the downs","His Bishop sacrifice headed into town"]],["h",3,"The Aftermath – The Jester speaks","the-aftermath-the-jester-speaks",0],["p","Inevitable, you say? Yes, blindness has its price. But so does speaking the truth.",0],["s",353,["The King has fled, the Bishop’s dead","The Chamberlain has lost","The message sent has torn a rent","As mothers count the cost"]],["s",357,["For so it is—you hit, you miss","And lose your only child","Though dead he be, don’t look to me","The Jester can’t be riled"]],["s",361,["My clinging bells—the screams and yells","Are all in minor key","We lose, we win, I wear my grin","The truth will set us free"]],["h",3,"Epilogue","epilogue",0],["s",365,["Truth ever has a cost—","for the honest as for the liar—","but still we sing,","because we must,","because we are human"]],["h",2,"The Pilgrim","the-pilgrim",0],["p","So there is a price to pay for truth for the vulnerable, and there is a price for the mighty. But that’s not us, is it? Not you. Not me. As ordinary men and women, what can we do to face truths and yet live with ourselves? Let’s find out. ",0],["p",[["The Jester lights the lantern.",1]],1],["h",3,"Episode I – Departure","episode-i-departure",0],["s",370,["The Lord is my shepherd, I shall not want,","The Pilgrim said aloud and turned away","From everything she knew at Rue du Pont","And from the thought that she would rather stay","What lay ahead she knew not, but she prayed","Please let me come home safely from this quest","The glory be to you—then let me rest"]],["s",377,["A leg of lamb and two small loaves of bread","With anxious heart into a great unknown","There’s nothing for it but to go ahead","There’ll come a day they’ll say How you have grown","From what you learned and did—a girl, alone","It was not I, but God, here at my side","I trust in him; I’ll live—or I might die"]],["h",3,"Episode II – The Struggle and the Fall","episode-ii-the-struggle-and-the-fall",0],["s",384,["The road was long, for sleeping in the wild","She’d find a barn or a verderer’s hut","Asking for lodging, treated like a child","They all said no, with an if or a but","Blow after blow, in the pit of her gut","At last the shore, much later than she planned,","Where every ship rejected her offhand"]],["s",391,["Frustrated by the scoffs she searched in vain","When suddenly a man stood by her side","I’d like to help—you need it, that is plain","The ship I sail will not have you denied","She paid, relieved, and let him be her guide","Now hop aboard, he said and walked away","There was no fare, to him she was ’but prey"]],["h",3,"Episode III – Emergence","episode-iii-emergence",0],["s",398,["So deeply stranded in the town, and lost","A lonely pilgrim, tired and forlorn","A child that must be saved at any cost","So many lives, and all they know is scorn","If we should die, she thought, then who would mourn?","She kneeled by one and said I’m hungry too","Do you want help? Let’s see what we can do"]],["s",405,["The tavern’s lights were bright as they walked in","She meant to spend her last—this child must eat","But there, the thief; at dice and drinking gin","She snatched his dagger from behind his seat","He felt its point while getting on his feet","She took his purse but cut one coin in two","I’ll keep the knife so that belongs to you"]],["h",3,"Episode IV – Realisation","episode-iv-realisation",0],["s",412,["A voice in her head said what have you done?","A likely future, echoes from her past","To take her fate into her hands and run","When thinking of that choice, she stopped and gasped","And then sped on, towards the quay at last","She chose a ship, the child clutched to her breast","A pilgrim pair, so far from being blessed"]],["s",419,["Hands down, the sailor laughed, that is so good","Easily the funniest tale I’ve heard","You took your money back because you could","But wondered if you should—that’s too absurd","One mustn’t treat you like a fool, my word!","You saved a child while at the edge of life",[["Not only that, you also ",0],["bought ",1],["his knife!",0]]]],["h",3,"Episode V – Arrival","episode-v-arrival",0],["s",426,["Tell me Pilgrim, what do we do now?","The child beside her, peering at the shore","You’re strong and kind, there is wisdom on your brow","We will get by, the fear I had before","Is gone by you, I doubt not anymore","The Pilgrim nodded—yes, my child, it’s true","We’ve come this far, we’ve made it—me and you"]],["s",433,["And so it was, before she saw the church","She knew that she had reached her journey’s end","There was no further need for any search","Noone but her on who she must depend","That all the blessings looked-for were pretend","Standing on the prow with wind in her hair","Almost within touch of Bælwythe, the fair"]],["h",1,"Scene IV Farewell","scene-iv-farewell",0],["p","It is time for this fool to say goodbye. My merry bites have kept us long enough.",0],["h",2,"The Jester speaks","the-jester-speaks",0],["s",440,["It takes a fool to tell a tale like ours","To whisper truths we must not disregard","A town there was, complete with walls and towers","So strong and proud yet only a façade","Come learn to see the limit of their power","Pray silence for the fool, the roguish bard","A tale of wit and jest in slanted rhyme","How truth is shaped, a story old as time"]],["p",[["The lights slowly fade to black, the Jester is standing still with his lantern. After a little while in darkness, he puts the lantern out.",1]],1]]}};
